––– comment –––
Synchronous OPTIMIZE TABLE on a distributed table fans out to every local
component and every non-blackhole remote mirror. Internal optimize requests
carry mandatory same-socket heartbeats so work can outlive the original agent
query lease. The 200 ms timeout below is a deterministic transport oracle.

––– input –––
export INSTANCE=1
––– output –––
––– block: ../../base/replication/start-searchd-precach –––
––– input –––
export INSTANCE=2
––– output –––
––– block: ../../base/replication/start-searchd-precach –––
––– input –––
export INSTANCE=3
––– output –––
––– block: ../../base/replication/start-searchd-precach –––
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "SET GLOBAL auto_optimize=0;"; mysql -h0 -P2306 -e "SET GLOBAL auto_optimize=0;"; mysql -h0 -P3306 -e "SET GLOBAL auto_optimize=0;"
––– output –––
––– comment –––
The regular SQL statement requires sync=1 before any target can be mutated.
The successful request must run longer than its original 200 ms lease, compact
the remote table, and complete through the streamed heartbeat transport.
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P2306 -e "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS remote_reply_rt; CREATE TABLE remote_reply_rt(title text) optimize_cutoff='1'; INSERT INTO remote_reply_rt VALUES(1,'one'),(2,'two'); FLUSH RAMCHUNK remote_reply_rt; INSERT INTO remote_reply_rt VALUES(3,'three'),(4,'four'); FLUSH RAMCHUNK remote_reply_rt;"; mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS remote_reply_dist; CREATE TABLE remote_reply_dist TYPE='distributed' AGENT='127.0.0.1:2312:remote_reply_rt' agent_query_timeout='200ms';"
––– output –––
––– input –––
out=$(mysql --force -h0 -P1306 -e "OPTIMIZE TABLE remote_reply_dist OPTION cutoff=1" 2>&1 || true); chunks=$(mysql -h0 -P2306 -e "SHOW TABLE remote_reply_rt STATUS LIKE 'disk_chunks'" | awk -F'|' '$2 ~ /disk_chunks/ {gsub(/ /,"",$3); print $3}'); if printf '%s\n' "$out" | grep -q "requires OPTION sync=1" && [ "$chunks" = 2 ]; then echo SYNC_REQUIRED_BEFORE_MUTATION; else printf 'FAIL_SYNC_REQUIRED chunks=%s error=%s\n' "$chunks" "$out"; fi
––– output –––
SYNC_REQUIRED_BEFORE_MUTATION
––– input –––
started_ms=$(date +%s%3N); if mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "OPTIMIZE TABLE remote_reply_dist OPTION sync=1,cutoff=1"; then optimize_ok=1; else optimize_ok=0; fi; elapsed_ms=$(( $(date +%s%3N)-started_ms )); chunks=$(mysql -h0 -P2306 -e "SHOW TABLE remote_reply_rt STATUS LIKE 'disk_chunks'" | awk -F'|' '$2 ~ /disk_chunks/ {gsub(/ /,"",$3); print $3}'); if [ "$optimize_ok" = 1 ] && [ "$elapsed_ms" -gt 200 ] && [ "$chunks" = 1 ]; then printf 'DISTRIBUTED_HEARTBEAT_OK elapsed_ms=%s\n' "$elapsed_ms"; else printf 'FAIL_DISTRIBUTED_HEARTBEAT ok=%s elapsed_ms=%s chunks=%s\n' "$optimize_ok" "$elapsed_ms" "$chunks"; fi
––– output –––
DISTRIBUTED_HEARTBEAT_OK elapsed_ms=%{NUMBER}
––– comment –––
A mixed distributed table must optimize its local component and every physical
table named by an agent. The cutoff is shared across the whole request.
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS optimize_local; CREATE TABLE optimize_local(title text) optimize_cutoff='1'; INSERT INTO optimize_local VALUES(1,'one'); FLUSH RAMCHUNK optimize_local; INSERT INTO optimize_local VALUES(2,'two'); FLUSH RAMCHUNK optimize_local;"; mysql -h0 -P2306 -e "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS optimize_remote_a; DROP TABLE IF EXISTS optimize_remote_b; CREATE TABLE optimize_remote_a(title text) optimize_cutoff='1'; CREATE TABLE optimize_remote_b(title text) optimize_cutoff='1'; INSERT INTO optimize_remote_a VALUES(1,'one'); FLUSH RAMCHUNK optimize_remote_a; INSERT INTO optimize_remote_a VALUES(2,'two'); FLUSH RAMCHUNK optimize_remote_a; INSERT INTO optimize_remote_b VALUES(1,'one'); FLUSH RAMCHUNK optimize_remote_b; INSERT INTO optimize_remote_b VALUES(2,'two'); FLUSH RAMCHUNK optimize_remote_b;"; mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS optimize_mixed; CREATE TABLE optimize_mixed TYPE='distributed' LOCAL='optimize_local' AGENT='127.0.0.1:2312:optimize_remote_a,optimize_remote_b' agent_query_timeout='2s'; OPTIMIZE TABLE optimize_mixed OPTION sync=1,cutoff=1;"
––– output –––
––– input –––
local_chunks=$(mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "SHOW TABLE optimize_local STATUS LIKE 'disk_chunks'" | awk -F'|' '$2 ~ /disk_chunks/ {gsub(/ /,"",$3); print $3}'); a_chunks=$(mysql -h0 -P2306 -e "SHOW TABLE optimize_remote_a STATUS LIKE 'disk_chunks'" | awk -F'|' '$2 ~ /disk_chunks/ {gsub(/ /,"",$3); print $3}'); b_chunks=$(mysql -h0 -P2306 -e "SHOW TABLE optimize_remote_b STATUS LIKE 'disk_chunks'" | awk -F'|' '$2 ~ /disk_chunks/ {gsub(/ /,"",$3); print $3}'); if [ "$local_chunks" = 1 ] && [ "$a_chunks" = 1 ] && [ "$b_chunks" = 1 ]; then echo MIXED_MULTI_TARGET_OK; else echo "FAIL_MIXED_MULTI_TARGET local=$local_chunks a=$a_chunks b=$b_chunks"; fi
––– output –––
MIXED_MULTI_TARGET_OK
––– comment –––
Every physical target is resolved as an RT table before the agent starts the
sequence. A later percolate target therefore rejects the request while the
earlier valid RT target still has both disk chunks.
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P2306 -e "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS optimize_validate_rt; DROP TABLE IF EXISTS optimize_validate_pq; CREATE TABLE optimize_validate_rt(title text) optimize_cutoff='1'; CREATE TABLE optimize_validate_pq(title text, meta json) type='pq'; INSERT INTO optimize_validate_rt VALUES(1,'one'); FLUSH RAMCHUNK optimize_validate_rt; INSERT INTO optimize_validate_rt VALUES(2,'two'); FLUSH RAMCHUNK optimize_validate_rt;"; mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS optimize_validate; CREATE TABLE optimize_validate TYPE='distributed' AGENT='127.0.0.1:2312:optimize_validate_rt,optimize_validate_pq' agent_query_timeout='2s';"
––– output –––
––– input –––
out=$(mysql --force -h0 -P1306 -e "OPTIMIZE TABLE optimize_validate OPTION sync=1,cutoff=1" 2>&1 || true); chunks=$(mysql -h0 -P2306 -e "SHOW TABLE optimize_validate_rt STATUS LIKE 'disk_chunks'" | awk -F'|' '$2 ~ /disk_chunks/ {gsub(/ /,"",$3); print $3}'); if printf '%s\n' "$out" | grep -q "remote table 'optimize_validate_pq' must be an existing RT table" && [ "$chunks" = 2 ]; then echo ALL_REMOTE_TARGETS_VALIDATED_BEFORE_MUTATION; else printf 'FAIL_REMOTE_TARGET_VALIDATION chunks=%s error=%s\n' "$chunks" "$out"; fi
––– output –––
ALL_REMOTE_TARGETS_VALIDATED_BEFORE_MUTATION
––– comment –––
GetAllHosts() intentionally schedules every mirror for distributed optimize,
instead of choosing one mirror as a normal search would.
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P2306 -e "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS optimize_mirror; CREATE TABLE optimize_mirror(title text) optimize_cutoff='1'; INSERT INTO optimize_mirror VALUES(1,'one'); FLUSH RAMCHUNK optimize_mirror; INSERT INTO optimize_mirror VALUES(2,'two'); FLUSH RAMCHUNK optimize_mirror;"; mysql -h0 -P3306 -e "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS optimize_mirror; CREATE TABLE optimize_mirror(title text) optimize_cutoff='1'; INSERT INTO optimize_mirror VALUES(1,'one'); FLUSH RAMCHUNK optimize_mirror; INSERT INTO optimize_mirror VALUES(2,'two'); FLUSH RAMCHUNK optimize_mirror;"; mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS optimize_all_mirrors; CREATE TABLE optimize_all_mirrors TYPE='distributed' AGENT='127.0.0.1:2312:optimize_mirror|127.0.0.1:3312:optimize_mirror' agent_query_timeout='2s'; OPTIMIZE TABLE optimize_all_mirrors OPTION sync=1,cutoff=1;"
––– output –––
––– input –––
mirror_a=$(mysql -h0 -P2306 -e "SHOW TABLE optimize_mirror STATUS LIKE 'disk_chunks'" | awk -F'|' '$2 ~ /disk_chunks/ {gsub(/ /,"",$3); print $3}'); mirror_b=$(mysql -h0 -P3306 -e "SHOW TABLE optimize_mirror STATUS LIKE 'disk_chunks'" | awk -F'|' '$2 ~ /disk_chunks/ {gsub(/ /,"",$3); print $3}'); if [ "$mirror_a" = 1 ] && [ "$mirror_b" = 1 ]; then echo ALL_MIRRORS_OK; else echo "FAIL_ALL_MIRRORS first=$mirror_a second=$mirror_b"; fi
––– output –––
ALL_MIRRORS_OK
––– comment –––
Runtime failures are strict but do not roll back completed work. Both remote
hosts are scheduled together, both errors are reported, and the local member
that completed before those failures remains compacted.
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS optimize_partial_local; CREATE TABLE optimize_partial_local(title text) optimize_cutoff='1'; INSERT INTO optimize_partial_local VALUES(1,'one'); FLUSH RAMCHUNK optimize_partial_local; INSERT INTO optimize_partial_local VALUES(2,'two'); FLUSH RAMCHUNK optimize_partial_local; DROP TABLE IF EXISTS optimize_partial; CREATE TABLE optimize_partial TYPE='distributed' LOCAL='optimize_partial_local' AGENT='127.0.0.1:2312:optimize_missing_a' AGENT='127.0.0.1:3312:optimize_missing_b' agent_query_timeout='2s';"
––– output –––
––– input –––
out=$(mysql --force -h0 -P1306 -e "OPTIMIZE TABLE optimize_partial OPTION sync=1,cutoff=1" 2>&1 || true); local_chunks=$(mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "SHOW TABLE optimize_partial_local STATUS LIKE 'disk_chunks'" | awk -F'|' '$2 ~ /disk_chunks/ {gsub(/ /,"",$3); print $3}'); if printf '%s\n' "$out" | grep -q 'optimize_missing_a' && printf '%s\n' "$out" | grep -q 'optimize_missing_b' && [ "$local_chunks" = 1 ]; then echo STRICT_PARTIAL_FAILURE_OK; else printf 'FAIL_STRICT_PARTIAL_FAILURE chunks=%s error=%s\n' "$local_chunks" "$out"; fi
––– output –––
STRICT_PARTIAL_FAILURE_OK
––– comment –––
The public shard-write path remains unchanged and continues to accept a short
request with the streamed SHARD_WRITE transport.
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P2306 -e "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS remote_reply_shard_rt; CREATE TABLE remote_reply_shard_rt(id bigint, title text, gid uint);"
––– output –––
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS remote_reply_shard; CREATE TABLE remote_reply_shard(id bigint, title text, gid uint) TYPE='shard' AGENT='127.0.0.1:2312:remote_reply_shard_rt';"
––– output –––
––– input –––
if mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "INSERT INTO remote_reply_shard(id,title,gid) VALUES(101,'short-a',11),(102,'short-b',22)"; then echo SHORT_SHARD_TERMINAL_OK; else echo FAIL_SHORT_SHARD_TERMINAL; fi
––– output –––
SHORT_SHARD_TERMINAL_OK
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P2306 -e "SELECT id,title,gid FROM remote_reply_shard_rt WHERE id=101; SELECT id,title,gid FROM remote_reply_shard_rt WHERE id=102" | awk -F'|' 'BEGIN{OFS="\t"} /^[|]/{for(i=2;i<=4;i++) gsub(/^ +| +$/,"",$i); if ($2!="" && $2!="id") print $2,$3,$4}'
––– output –––
101	short-a	11
102	short-b	22
––– comment –––
Synchronous OPTIMIZE on type='shard' enters the same routed fan-out path as a
distributed table. The remote physical target is the oracle for native routing.
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P2306 -e "TRUNCATE TABLE remote_reply_shard_rt; INSERT INTO remote_reply_shard_rt(id,title,gid) VALUES(201,'chunk-a',31); FLUSH RAMCHUNK remote_reply_shard_rt; INSERT INTO remote_reply_shard_rt(id,title,gid) VALUES(202,'chunk-b',32); FLUSH RAMCHUNK remote_reply_shard_rt;"; chunks=$(mysql -h0 -P2306 -e "SHOW TABLE remote_reply_shard_rt STATUS LIKE 'disk_chunks'" | awk -F'|' '$2 ~ /disk_chunks/ {gsub(/ /,"",$3); print $3}'); if [ "$chunks" = 2 ]; then echo SHARD_OPTIMIZE_PREPARED; else echo "FAIL_SHARD_OPTIMIZE_PREPARED chunks=$chunks"; fi
––– output –––
SHARD_OPTIMIZE_PREPARED
––– input –––
if mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "OPTIMIZE TABLE remote_reply_shard OPTION sync=1,cutoff=1"; then optimize_ok=1; else optimize_ok=0; fi; chunks=$(mysql -h0 -P2306 -e "SHOW TABLE remote_reply_shard_rt STATUS LIKE 'disk_chunks'" | awk -F'|' '$2 ~ /disk_chunks/ {gsub(/ /,"",$3); print $3}'); if [ "$optimize_ok" = 1 ] && [ "$chunks" = 1 ]; then echo SHARD_SYNC_OPTIMIZE_OK; else echo "FAIL_SHARD_SYNC_OPTIMIZE ok=$optimize_ok chunks=$chunks"; fi
––– output –––
SHARD_SYNC_OPTIMIZE_OK
